{"event_type":"review","id":"499065c2417e43ecb2275615a4e8e71bf7afd2ea4ff8be3f1ed867ab8dae2a80","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T23:27:11Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7addc4de3ed38a525dee5aabce304c2c1e3da9b3cc964f1ac083a6f55838daa1","sha256":"7addc4de3ed38a525dee5aabce304c2c1e3da9b3cc964f1ac083a6f55838daa1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b843d000253c66aee3e6aec704eb3c2730bf6d8cf69d55ecba0d6b481cbd987e","sha256":"b843d000253c66aee3e6aec704eb3c2730bf6d8cf69d55ecba0d6b481cbd987e"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/40bef3e7fed2c651ffdffcef1537e88b91f4183be3866f7420cbb159dc31f08a","sha256":"40bef3e7fed2c651ffdffcef1537e88b91f4183be3866f7420cbb159dc31f08a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/abc82b9e029bf8adebae9060254e2bd6bc103acdf7e7db85caaf0ec4170a3538","sha256":"abc82b9e029bf8adebae9060254e2bd6bc103acdf7e7db85caaf0ec4170a3538"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/490c25b4cf2ff7c3f57c83e0f4db7a42e87e947a76eeb4b6e521a0e7225f9fa9","sha256":"490c25b4cf2ff7c3f57c83e0f4db7a42e87e947a76eeb4b6e521a0e7225f9fa9"}],"attempt_id":"6e55088580a37805abe2ad87aeb230ccdc3c8cee11c9ac55729b10fe5176cd56:0:1","base":"061e01447e22dc838fad428a752ddafad3d6bf58","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"8242fffeed91c59d76a6f4e96e9728e4bb3493a2","body":"**Strip an inherited `GH_REPO` from the default gh runner.**\n\nLine 59 builds the runner with `cwd` only. The `makeGhRunner` doc in `src/adapters/forge-github/gh.ts` says gh resolves the repo as `-R` > `GH_REPO` > cwd. It also says a cwd-scoped runner must strip an inherited `GH_REPO`.\n\nIf `GH_REPO` is set in the environment, `gh repo view` on Line 76 returns that repo, not the `repoRoot` remote. The check on Lines 77-83 then passes without testing `repoRoot`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    const gh = deps.gh ?? makeGhRunner({ cwd: input.repoRoot, timeoutMs: 30_000 });\n+    const gh =\n+      deps.gh ??\n+      makeGhRunner({ cwd: input.repoRoot, timeoutMs: 30_000, unsetEnv: ['GH_REPO'] });\n```\n</details>","id":"6358df2a2ef74d969a6e0d4c3eddbe5e37f80d4081ca3e90915258985dbe9baa","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/addressMany.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Strip an inherited `GHREPO` from the default gh runner."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"8242fffeed91c59d76a6f4e96e9728e4bb3493a2","body":"**Pass the selected head to `address`.**\n\nIf the PR head changes after revalidation, `address` can apply and push fixes on the new head. The aggregate detects a mismatched admission head only after the run.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n           result = await address({\n             repoRoot: input.repoRoot,\n             source: `pr:${candidate.number}`,\n+            expectedHead: candidate.headOid,\n             maxTokens: input.tokensPerPr,\n```\n\n</details>","id":"8be190813c755013555ce9e6761527f3b336e660879390e14faa31298269dd98","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/addressMany.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Pass the selected head to `address`."}],"head":"8b46a6bb564e2bc6cfe34e4afe8f7ca1ea9176ed","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"8242fffeed91c59d76a6f4e96e9728e4bb3493a2","intervals":[[1,205]],"path":"src/ops/review/addressMany.ts"},{"blob":"7953c966f55ab81afe81c16fa5e6878740fedef1","intervals":[[1,200]],"path":"src/ops/review/planReviewBatch.ts"}],"job_id":"6e55088580a37805abe2ad87aeb230ccdc3c8cee11c9ac55729b10fe5176cd56:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"8242fffeed91c59d76a6f4e96e9728e4bb3493a2","disposition":"included","mode":"